=== CORRECTION 2026-08-25 (re-review N1) — appended, log body NOT rewritten
Line 6 of this log and the script header above call tb/scripts/model_v2_s1.txt
"the committed 0.8B stream".  It is NOT committed: `.gitignore:13`
(`tb/scripts/model_*`) excludes it, because it is ~45 MB of a ~950 MB artifact
set, and `git ls-files` does not know it.

The accurate label is stronger than the wrong one, which is why this is a
correction and not a retraction of the census:

  * the file is GITIGNORED, on disk only; but
  * `ref/scripts/regen_gate.sh` BYTE-LOCKS exactly this artifact.  It re-emits
    from committed sources, checks sha256(model_v2_s1.e.seq) against the frozen
    GOLD_SEQ_SHA=a69864d25b6b129a4d6c74b3c78dfcbedf1edce219d32cc05d05bc54f444aaf1
    (regen_gate.sh:5, :38-40), and then runs
        cmp $TMP/model_v2_s1.txt ../tb/scripts/model_v2_s1.txt
    (regen_gate.sh:41), failing REGEN_GATE_FAIL_TXT on any difference.

So from a clean checkout, `make -C tb model_script_s1` (or the gate itself)
reproduces this exact input byte-for-byte, and the gate PROVES it did.  The
census numbers below — 288 DNST commands per token = 18 DN layers x 16 heads,
576 length-128 VN = 18 x 16 x 2 — are unchanged and are reproducible from
committed sources.
